  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: DarkTrack
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: dark_track
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 1
  _narratorPrompt: Three on the branch, right there in the light, easy to count. On the main line, the track runs off into the dark, and I swear to you there is a crowd tied up out there in the black. How many. That would be telling. Could be one, could be a whole coachload. Divert, and you kill three you can see, for certain. Leave it, and you gamble against a number I refuse to give you. Trust me, or trust your eyes. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: You pulled. Three folded, quick and certain, done. And now the main line, with the dark thinned away to nothing. Look at it. Empty rail, all the way down. Not one soul was ever out there. You killed three real people to swerve a crowd I invented on the spot. Oh, that is delicious.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 39
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact: []
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. The cart rolled off into all that darkness I swore was packed with souls, and struck nobody, because there was nobody. Look, the black has cleared. Empty the whole time. You stood there and sweated over a crowd that never existed. I do love this one.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 61
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact: []
